## Quick Command Reference

### Workflow Development

```bash
# Check status
python cli/status.py my-workflow

# Validate locally
python cli/test_wdl_action.py my-workflow --local-only

# Test remotely
python cli/test_wdl_action.py my-workflow

# Save draft
python cli/save_wdl_draft.py --workflow-id my-workflow

# Publish
python cli/publish_wdl_action.py --workflow-id my-workflow
```

### Remote Action Editing

```bash
# List all remote actions
python cli/discover.py --list-all

# Download action to local workspace
python cli/checkout_wdl_version.py --workflow-id <action-id>

# Edit widdle.json, then test
python cli/test_wdl_action.py <action-id> --local-only
python cli/test_wdl_action.py <action-id> --all

# Push new version
python cli/save_wdl_draft.py --workflow-id <action-id>
python cli/publish_wdl_action.py --workflow-id <action-id>
```

### Workspace Management

```bash
# Environment
python cli/workspace.py env create --id staging --name "Staging" --use
python cli/workspace.py env list

# Agent
python cli/workspace.py agent create --id my-agent --name "My Agent"
python cli/workspace.py agent checkout --remote-id abc123 --env staging --include-subactions

# Action
python cli/workspace.py action create --id my-action --title "My Action"
```

### Testing

```bash
# Single action
python cli/test_wdl_action.py my-action

# Parallel
python cli/test_runner.py action1 action2 action3 --parallel 3

# All in environment
python cli/test_runner.py --workspace production-client-a

# Via-agent (sub-action through agent)
python cli/test_runner.py my-agent --via-agent --subaction get-data
```

### Tool Mode (for sub-actions)

```bash
python cli/deployment_rules.py my-action --enable-tool-mode
python cli/deployment_rules.py my-action --show
```

### Discovery (`cli/discover.py`)

```bash
# List by type
python cli/discover.py --list-tools         # Tools only
python cli/discover.py --list-all           # All actions
python cli/discover.py --list-workflows     # Workflows only
python cli/discover.py --list-apis          # Available APIs

# Semantic search
python cli/discover.py --actions "inventory"
python cli/discover.py --apis "auth"

# Fuzzy search (for specific names)
python cli/discover.py --actions "get-orderpoints" --mode fuzzy

# From requirements file
python cli/discover.py --requirements requirements.md

# Verbose debugging
python cli/discover.py --list-tools --verbose

# JSON output
python cli/discover.py --actions "query" --json
```

